  "slug": "quantum-circuit-compilation-0208",
  "summary": "New preprints tie compilation to hardware cost metrics, reporting gains over Qiskit O3 and EPOC baselines and cutting QAOA two-qubit depth.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is compilation guided by hardware-level cost rather than abstract gate count. SCOPE uses an operator Schmidt time surrogate to reduce pulse execution latency and reports gains over EPOC on 104 benchmarks. The quspect SDK selects routings after coupling-constrained resynthesis, reaching 0.616x Qiskit O3 two-qubit gates on 55 circuits across five targets. For Max-Cut QAOA on non-native graphs, MinLA surrogates prune interactions to lower two-qubit depth, and classical configuration recovery follows. CAVQS adds variational synthesis with unitary redistribution and mid-circuit dynamic reconstruction. Adjacent items on speed limits, QSVT inversion degree, and quantum Hamiltonian descent are algorithmic or theoretical neighbors rather than compilation results.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
